WEBVTT


00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.580
Let me just say this. You want to be the beneficiary.

00:00:03.581 --> 00:00:05.800
No other title actually matters

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.680
because equity sees the beneficiary as the true owner of the trust,

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.680
not trustee, not executor, beneficiary.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.040
There are two parties I wanna focus on,

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.040
trust and estates. The estate gets charged, right,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.680
and the trust settles the charges, right?

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.860
You are the beneficiary, meaning

00:00:24.861 --> 00:00:26.380
the trust works in your favour

00:00:26.381 --> 00:00:30.680
to stop you from being held as surety for charges against the estate.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.820
This is why the trust is so important.

00:00:32.821 --> 00:00:36.440
It stops you from paying debt that are not your responsibility.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.000
Because if there's no money and we've been in bankruptcy since 1933,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.700
all we have to do is accept the charges against the estate

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.240
and discharge them in trust.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.800
So can we please live like we know what to do in 2026?
